  "key_finding": "The rule-based verifier is structurally direction-insensitive: reversing the citation edge for an originally-supported dependency-relation claim flips the verdict only 19.1% of the time (0% for compares/shares_topic), because the decision rule accepts a citation link in EITHER direction as support (Eq. 14: c_BA=1 alone suffices). This means the current verifier cannot detect a claim that gets the citation DIRECTION backwards (e.g. \"A builds on B\" when actually \"B builds on A\") as long as some edge connects them -- a real, previously unstated limitation that directly motivates direction-reversal hard negatives (item 4) and a learned verifier with an explicit direction-aware feature (item 1)."
